# Cloud Composer: 
Best for heavy, data-centric pipelines (MapReduce, Spark, Dataflow, complex ELT dependencies). It is cluster-backed (GKE) and has long task runtimes.

# Cloud Workflows: 
Best for lightweight, serverless, low-latency API orchestration. It chains HTTP-based services (Cloud Functions, Cloud Run, external webhooks) and costs practically nothing when idle.
low-latency HTTP service orchestration

# The KubernetesPodOperator (KPO) 
Standard PythonOperator tasks run inline on the main Airflow worker pods. If a task runs heavy processing or has conflicting third-party library versions (e.g., Pandas 1.x vs 2.x), do not use PythonOperator.
conflicting Python libraries inside Airflow

Concurrency Troubleshooting: If tasks are stuck in a queued or scheduled state indefinitely, but your underlying GKE cluster nodes show low CPU and RAM utilization, it is a software bottleneck. You must increase the ```parallelism``` and ```max_active_tasks_per_dag`` variables inside the airflow.cfg environment overrides.

# TestPipeline
Unit Testing: Use Apache Beam’s native TestPipeline class to validate transform math against local in-memory mock data. ```No GCP resources are deployed here```.

